### GET request to example server
GET https://examples.http-client.intellij.net/get
    ?generated-in=IntelliJ IDEA

### Signup a new member
POST http://localhost:3005/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberNick": "Ali",
  "memberPhone": "01058649977",
  "memberPassword": "1111111"
}

### Try the same again — should fail with "memberNick already taken"
POST http://localhost:3005/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberNick": "Ali",
  "memberPhone": "01058649977",
  "memberPassword": "1111111"
}

### Validation error — empty nick
POST http://localhost:3005/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberNick": "",
  "memberPhone": "+82-10-1111-2222",
  "memberPassword": "abc"
}

### 2. Login — capture the token
# @name login
POST http://localhost:3005/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberNick": "Sammy",
  "memberPassword": "1111111"
}

### 3. Use the token to access protected endpoint
@login =login
GET http://localhost:3005/members/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Without token — should fail with 403
GET http://localhost:3005/members/me

### 5. Wrong password — should fail with 401
POST http://localhost:3005/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "memberNick": "azamat",
  "memberPassword": "WRONG"
}